# Target C-II — retained-remainder floor on the Section-118 common-cap branch

**Date:** 2026-09-12  
**Status:** proof-only scoped Type-II tradeoff; theorem-state authority unchanged.  
**LEVEL I STATUS:** **STILL OPEN. C-II REMAINS OPEN.**

This note keeps the exact nonnegative component remainder in audited §161 and inserts
the independently audited Section-118 common-cap profile. It yields a stronger lower
bound for the Type-II density `t=(q-k)/D` on that scoped branch:

\[
\boxed{
\liminf_{D\to\infty}{q-k\over D}
\ge 1.8376645\ldots .
}
\tag{1}
\]

This is not a universal Type-II bound: the carrier area/moment inputs below are only
available on the repaired Section-118 endpoint/common-cap profile. The result does
not control separated wrapping parameters, the large-detour branch, or Type I.

## 1. Exact implication chain

Use

\[
t_D={q-k\over D},\qquad \kappa_D={k\over D},\qquad
S_D={1\over D}\sum_r d_r,\qquad G_D={G_D^{\rm fin}\over D}.
\]

Audited §161 gives the retained-remainder inequality

\[
5q-7k\ge 3\sum_r d_r+2G_D^{\rm fin}+c_*D-o(D),
\qquad
c_*={\pi\over4}(2-\sqrt3).
\tag{2}
\]

Since `q/D=t_D+\kappa_D` and `k/D=\kappa_D`, (2) is

\[
5t_D-2\kappa_D
\ge 3S_D+2G_D+c_*-o(1).
\tag{3}
\]

On the audited Section-118 common-cap profile, the same-component local area/slack
theorem and the diameter-moment theorem give

\[
S_D\ge S_*-o(1),\qquad S_*=2.798596312209462\ldots,
\tag{4}
\]

and

\[
G_D\ge G_*-o(1),\qquad G_*=0.2910434605114113\ldots.
\tag{5}
\]

Because `\kappa_D\ge0`, (3)--(5) imply

\[
\liminf t_D\ge
{3S_*+2G_*+c_*\over5}
=1.8376645322540885\ldots.
\tag{6}
\]

The key bookkeeping point is the coefficient: `5q-7k` becomes `5t-2\kappa`, while
the retained `G_D` term stays on the right. No h-only projection or sign reversal is
used.

## 2. Certified interval and regression

The accompanying verifier uses rational lower bounds for `S_*`, `G_*`, `\pi`, and
an upper bound for `\sqrt3` to certify

\[
{3S_*+2G_*+c_*\over5}>1.8376.
\]

It also checks the exact rational point

\[
t={37\over20},\quad \kappa=0,\quad S={14\over5},\quad G={3\over10},
\]

which lies above the scoped floor and satisfies the retained §161 inequality with a
strict margin. Thus this scalar strengthening does not itself close the branch; it
only moves the remaining feasible scalar region upward.

## 3. Scope and remaining obstruction

The conclusion is conditional on the same carrier/profile hypothesis used by the
audited local area/slack and diameter-moment modules. It retains all source points and
uses no affine-kernel statement for contact-isolated coordinates.

The large-detour/source-descent obligation remains: the five-currency bridge shows
that endpoint capacity can be paid by outer detour, while the present floor does not
turn that detour into a strict diameter decrease or an exact unit triangle. The
macroscopic inactive-container branch is untouched.

**Classification:** proved candidate awaiting independent audit; scoped to the
Section-118 common-cap Type-II profile; C-II remains open.
